WEBVTT

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.300
I like the circus.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:14.730
It amazes people and makes them smile.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.440
But I didn't know back then,

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.030
that there exists
a different kind of "circus."

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.450
One that spreads terror, not delight.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:07.740
Before dawn, when the stars paint the sky

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:12.870
I am searching for the thing I lost

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:17.710
With a restless heart
Under the sun yet in the dark

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:22.340
I patch together little prayers
to light my path

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:27.050
I don’t need anything,
as my hands are full

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.890
My hands are full of emptiness

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:36.640
Please, just once, nod for me

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.520
Just once, reach out to me like the mirror

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.360
I will live for that single moment,
that single second

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:51.030
All the rest can just burn away

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.660
What’s right for me is for me alone

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:00.580
Whatever the path, I'll follow it to you

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.250
This feeling grows and grows,
deep inside my heart

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:09.050
For one single reason

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:17.140
I continue to climb up on the stage

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:37.370
#1 The Curtain Rises

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:44.420
It's time to get warmed up.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.500
Coming.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.010
Step right up, step right up.
It's the famous Straw Circus.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:53.090
It's lots of fun.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:55.640
Only 3 stations from here.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.810
At the department store parking lot.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.350
Come see Straw Circus!

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:09.110
Step right up, step right up.
It's the famous Straw Circus.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:13.950
I'm sorry.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.410
Um, will you take me to the circus?

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:27.750
What, a runaway boy?

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:30.880
He looks well groomed.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.550
There must be a reason behind this.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:36.390
Stop, it's none of your business.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.890
Don't be a busybody.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.810
Huh? Come on...

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.900
Stop making me feel bad.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:53.820
Hey, you.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:06.790
Not now, not another seizure!

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.880
I've got to make somebody laugh. Anybody!

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.340
Laugh, please!

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:35.610
D-Damn it, I'm a goner now...

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.320
I...

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.170
Phew, that was close.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:02.930
You there. Wait, let me thank you.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:11.940
H-Help...!

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.190
Kidnappers?

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:21.700
Nobody else noticed it.
They've blocked him from view.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:23.450
What now?

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:26.540
They might be taking the runaway boy home.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:31.040
Aww, jeez.
I'll just apologize if I'm wrong!

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.840
Hey, you!

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.210
Were they kidnapping you?

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:45.350
Righty then, you're all going to the cops!

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:47.890
Oops, I went too far.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.570
Ow...! He's as strong as hell.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:03.320
What?

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.740
He dislocated his shoulder.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.580
It's not dislocated?

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.460
Who the hell are these guys?

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.090
Let's run!

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:22.130
Yeah, great idea.

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:37.530
Jeez, who were they?
They didn't even feel my punches.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.820
And they're as strong as hell.

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:44.160
You look a lot scarier
than I imagined you.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:48.740
Shut your face.
Who got me into this mess anyways, huh?

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.200
Sorry.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:54.580
Shoot, another attack.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.460
I really am sorry.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.050
Laugh.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.340
All because I spoke to you...

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:03.720
Just laugh.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:08.350
Laugh, or I'll knock your brains out!

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:10.810
I don't understand!

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:19.650
There, good.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:24.660
I'm Narumi Kato. You?

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:27.490
Masaru Saiga.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:30.120
I'm in 5th grade, sir.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.870
Sir, huh?
You from a rich family or something?

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:37.250
So, what the heck is going on?

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:44.090
Those men have been chasing me around
ever since my dad died.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:46.720
Ain't got no dad, huh?

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:50.680
Have you ever heard of "Saiga Group"?

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:53.180
What, Saiga?

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:56.650
That huge IT and automobile company?

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:02.110
My dad was the CEO.

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:05.320
Really? That's pretty awesome.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:08.320
You really are from a rich family.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:14.710
So the CEO of a huge company dies,

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:18.960
and some strange men are after the son.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:22.130
I hate to ask, but how did your dad die?

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.010
They said it was a car crash
on the highway.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.930
Something got caught in his tires.

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:32.350
What was it?

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:37.060
A puppet-like thing.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:44.360
And I remembered
what my late grandfather once told me.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:54.620
This is amazing, Grandpa.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:56.750
Surprised?

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:00.830
All the men in the Saiga family line
have a room like this.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.420
Dad too?

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:03.590
Of course.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:08.630
For some reason, all Saiga men
develop a keen interest in these.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:17.100
Puppets with clockwork innards
that make them move just like humans.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:19.730
We call them "Karakuri puppets."

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:26.360
This must be why the Saiga Group
excels at precision instruments.

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:31.160
The Saiga family's property
amounts to several billions.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:34.030
And it will all be yours someday.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:38.210
Yeah, Dad told me that before.
I don't really get it, though.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:41.750
No, of course not.

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:45.590
Nor the difficulties
it may cause you one day.

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:47.010
What do you mean?

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:53.760
Masaru, listen well to
what I have to tell you.

00:09:54.350 --> 00:10:00.270
If your dad should die before you grow up
and strange things begin to happen...

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:04.820
take that case and run away.

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:09.320
Shirogane will protect you.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:17.660
Who's Shirogane?

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.080
I don't know.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:25.670
But Grandpa said he or she'd always be
at the circus closest to me.

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:29.840
So that's why you were trying
to get to the circus.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:34.640
But you should go to the cops
and not the circus.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:38.850
Those men might be after your inheritance.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:40.600
No...

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:44.770
-He jumped on too, eh?
-Narumi.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.200
I know what you're after.

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:57.580
You asked for it now.

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:01.500
Have a taste of the martial arts
I learned in China.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:13.220
He's so strong.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.590
Hands off, you bastard!

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:19.930
Damn it.

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:27.400
I've got to get him someplace safe.

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:33.200
What now?

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:37.240
Are you crazy?

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:48.380
They're puppets?

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.760
Narumi, I'm sorry.

00:11:58.430 --> 00:12:00.600
I'm sorry I dragged you into this.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:02.390
The bear costume...

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:06.980
it looked so big and strong.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:11.400
I thought you might be able to save me.

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:13.900
That's why I came to you.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:19.450
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:21.450
Narumi...

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:28.290
I should've died alone
instead of dragging you into this.

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:35.050
Don't give up.
You didn't do anything wrong.

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:38.180
If you need help, shout for help.

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:40.390
If you're angry, speak out.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:45.310
Fight, struggle, do what you can.
And if all else fails...

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:49.100
I guess all you can do then is smile.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.160
Narumi!

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:15.710
Narumi...

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:24.310
That name... Shirogane?

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.480
Shirogane.

00:13:30.230 --> 00:13:33.860
It's no use.
There's no proof he or she even exists.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:37.320
I don't even know
what he or she looks like.

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:40.530
Don't give up!

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:46.750
Shirogane!

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:59.220
Shirogane?

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:09.850
Mister Masaru, stand back.

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:14.980
Arlequin!

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:40.510
Woah. Amazing.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.130
Is she...?

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:45.720
Are you Shirogane-san?

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:48.310
Are you okay, Mister Masaru?

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:51.940
Yeah. I mean, thanks.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:56.310
I'm so glad to finally be with you again.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:58.480
I can't breathe.

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:00.650
Forgive me.

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:03.660
That's a pretty cool puppet.

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:06.030
It brings back memories.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:10.040
Your grandfather called it Arlequin.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:15.080
Your grandfather hired my mother
when you two were in France.

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:17.540
She was your nanny.

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:21.720
But I've never been to France.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:25.590
It was 7 years ago, when you were only 4.

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:27.970
So you must not remember.

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:31.350
I was 11 then, too.

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:37.190
Your grandfather saved my mother and me
and gave us a proper living.

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:38.440
Ouch...

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:42.440
Damn, what are these things?

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:45.990
You're okay!

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:47.200
Wait!

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:49.790
Who are you?

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:52.660
She isn't Japanese.

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.170
Silver eyes.

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:57.290
Even her hair is silver.

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:01.960
But who cares about that.
This woman thinks I'm the enemy.

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:05.880
I was hired to work for this circus.
And who are you?

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:07.720
Masaru, don't trust her.

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:09.430
What is this puppet?

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.930
Puppets were what attacked Masaru,
you know.

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:16.350
Mister Masaru's grandfather
taught me to handle puppets.

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:19.860
He told me to protect him
should anything happen.

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:22.730
I practiced with this Arlequin then.

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:24.990
What is there to distrust?

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:28.450
Then where were you
when Masaru came running to me?

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:30.080
He was all alone!

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:33.370
I... I was...

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:35.160
Shut up!

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:40.960
Both of you, stop!

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:50.510
Mister Masaru!

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:53.180
No, Mister Masaru...

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:55.310
Forgive me.

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:56.770
I'll call an ambulance.

00:16:56.940 --> 00:16:58.650
No, it's not safe here.

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:06.240
What are you going to do?

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:08.240
I'll take him someplace safe.

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:12.030
Fine, I'll go with you then.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:15.120
No, this doesn't concern you anymore.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.540
I will protect him.

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:19.880
Return to your safe life.

00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:26.880
Oh well.

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:30.340
She doesn't seem like Masaru's enemy.

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:34.680
Besides, she's right.
It doesn't concern me.

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:37.180
Gotta stay out of these messes.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:42.730
I've got enough on my hands already.

00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:46.530
Like how I'll die
if I don't make people laugh.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:06.090
I guess they're going to keep causing
disasters like these,

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:08.760
just to get their hands on Masaru.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:16.350
How could I ever make people laugh
with that weighing on my conscience?

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:21.850
Besides, if things like these continue...

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:26.360
there'll be less and less people
who will laugh for me.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:34.070
You blew it? But he's just a boy.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:37.700
Yes, but there were a couple of intruders.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:39.080
Intruders?

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:42.830
One was just a passerby. A normal person.

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:47.090
But the other was one of us.
A puppet handler.

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:48.420
You don't mean...

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:49.760
Don't worry.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:51.630
I'll finish my job.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:56.640
But to do so, may I use "Pulcinella"?

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:12.650
Hey, you.

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.660
I knew it, you dumbass.
What are you doing?

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.450
What were you going to do, huh?

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:22.960
The hospitals were closed.
I want to go to the emergency room but...

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:27.880
Duh, it's Sunday. And no taxi would stop
for someone dressed like that.

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:30.880
Thinking you can do everything
by yourself.

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:32.010
Come on.

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:33.300
Don't touch that!

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:39.310
This is my town. I know a doc nearby.

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:44.690
Think of Masaru!
It's our fault he's like that.

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:53.400
Come on.

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:55.660
"SUGANO HOSPITAL"

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:58.700
Darn you, calling on me at all hours
all the time.

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:00.540
Thanks, Doc.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:03.960
The bumps aren't much
but he got 5 stitches in his arm.

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.790
I won't ask what happened,
but take it easy.

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:09.210
Thank you so much.

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:11.000
It's nothing.

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:13.800
She's a real hottie.

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:16.220
Your late grandpa would be proud.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:17.890
It's not like that.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:21.720
We hate each other if you must know.

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:31.230
That boy doesn't think so.

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:35.490
I'll be upstairs.
Let him sleep awhile before going home.

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:37.030
Don't forget his meds.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:38.410
Yeah.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:46.660
Why did you come for us?

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:51.800
You still don't trust me, huh.

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:56.550
Rest easy.
It wasn't for you or for Masaru.

00:20:59.140 --> 00:21:00.350
I did it for myself.

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:04.270
If I ignored him, I wouldn't be able
to sleep nights.

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:07.560
I only think about myself, got it?

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:13.360
And what you said before is dead wrong.
My life is far from safe.

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:15.900
I wanted to set that straight!

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:18.360
Listen here, I've got this disease...

00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:32.790
Arlequin!

00:21:37.090 --> 00:21:39.050
I couldn't care less about your disease,

00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:42.720
but I understand your reason for coming.

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:44.810
For yourself.

00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:46.390
Right?

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:47.810
That's right.

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:50.440
It's for myself.

00:21:54.690 --> 00:21:57.940
I didn't know it then.

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:02.870
But for Shirogane, Narumi, and me,

00:22:03.030 --> 00:22:08.080
the colossal wheels of destiny
were slowly beginning to turn.

00:22:14.630 --> 00:22:16.960
Fly up high, Marionette

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:19.260
Turn to ash, gracefully

00:22:19.420 --> 00:22:23.760
My only purpose in life was to fight

00:22:23.930 --> 00:22:28.430
Why am I so angry
even I dump my humanity

00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:34.560
Without you, I can’t smile anymore

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:40.110
I assume that I am to be blamed

00:22:40.280 --> 00:22:44.320
Like a puppet that can’t smile naturally

00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:49.660
I feel like someone is pulling my strings

00:22:49.870 --> 00:22:53.460
What am I even living for?

00:22:53.670 --> 00:22:57.750
I was hurt, and thought
that nobody would understand

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:02.840
But you came along,
and took me in your arms

00:23:03.050 --> 00:23:09.100
I felt my tangled arms and legs

00:23:09.430 --> 00:23:11.310
become free

00:23:11.770 --> 00:23:14.150
Fly up high, Marionette

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:16.360
I think now I can reach you

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:20.900
Before I met you, I was empty

00:23:21.150 --> 00:23:25.700
Now I have something
I'd give my all to protect

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:32.080
You taught me how to feel,
the feeling of sorrow too
